WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.010
Managed Apps change the picture.

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:08.850
A maker can build one in Copilot Cowork, in Copilot Studio, or with the Managed Apps CLI.

00:00:10.019 --> 00:00:11.228
Wherever it's built,

00:00:11.238 --> 00:00:15.749
the source code lands in a Git repository that Microsoft manages for you.

00:00:16.339 --> 00:00:18.789
Each deploy is a commit, built in the cloud.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.170
The finished app runs on the Copilot Managed Runtime:

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:24.630
one shared host for every app.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:27.170
It doesn't live inside an environment.

00:00:28.173 --> 00:00:29.823
But it is still governed by one.

00:00:30.373 --> 00:00:34.523
Every app is pinned to a Power Platform environment, once, when it's created.

00:00:35.458 --> 00:00:39.477
If no environment is given, as when the app skill in Cowork builds it,

00:00:39.487 --> 00:00:43.228
the app is pinned to the maker's personal developer environment.

00:00:43.858 --> 00:00:46.668
Name an environment, and it's pinned there instead.

00:00:47.693 --> 00:00:49.443
That environment sets the rules:

00:00:49.933 --> 00:00:53.025
which connectors are allowed, the connections it uses,

00:00:53.035 --> 00:00:58.263
its Dataverse data and security roles, who it can be shared with, and what admins can see.
